### Try the API (VS Code REST Client or Visual Studio). Start it with: dotnet run --project src/PayableFlow.Api
@host = http://localhost:5000

### Create a vendor with "2/10 Net 30" terms
POST {{host}}/vendors
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Acme Supplies", "paymentTermsDays": 30, "earlyDiscountPercent": 2, "earlyDiscountDays": 10 }

### Enter a bill
POST {{host}}/invoices
Content-Type: application/json

{ "vendorId": 1, "invoiceNumber": "INV-1001", "amount": 1200.00 }

### Same bill again with a typo in the number: rejected as a possible duplicate
POST {{host}}/invoices
Content-Type: application/json

{ "vendorId": 1, "invoiceNumber": "INV1001", "amount": 1200.00 }

### Aging report
GET {{host}}/reports/aging

### Plan a payment run with limited cash
POST {{host}}/payment-runs/plan
Content-Type: application/json

{ "budget": 5000 }

### Three-way match
POST {{host}}/matching
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "order":    [ { "sku": "LAP-15", "quantity": 10, "unitPrice": 1000 } ],
  "receipts": [ { "sku": "LAP-15", "quantity": 6 } ],
  "invoice":  [ { "sku": "LAP-15", "quantity": 10, "unitPrice": 1000 } ]
}
